        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRENGCON.—THE SANITARY WORKS COMMITTER of the Council of the Borough invite Tenders for the supply of about 35 tons per week of Washed Slack, of good quality, to be delivered at Longford Depot in such quantities as may be required from day to day, during the next three or six months. Tenderers must submit along with their tender, a 71b. sample of the washed el tett they ten ler for, and must name the pit from which the slack will be taken. The Contractors shall psy all persons engaged or employed by them on the works the rate of wages recognised in the district, and shall observe such hours of labour as are Remerally accepted as fair in each trade, and shall from time to time, whenever required so to do by the Council. produce to them such evidence as they may deem sufficient that they are paying such wages and observing such hours. Tenders to be addressed to "The Chairman. Sanitary Works Committee. Town trail, Warrington" to be securely fastened, endor.ed '' Tender for Slack "and delivered not later than 10 a.m. on Tuesday, September 29th, 1993. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accented. JAMES DEAS. Water and Sanitary Rnspineer. Municipal Offices, Warrineon, September 18th 19)3.</p>
