        <head>PRETTY EODICE:</head>
        <p>A PRETTY EODICE:</p>
        <p>quite closely at the sides, while as a general rule the fronts pouch slightly, the fulling starting from the short yoke of lace or embroidery. A blouse to prove a satisfac- tory possession should be made to order, as there is a wide difference between one which is specially cut and fitted to the figure of the wearer and a ready - made article which flaunts its origin all over it and requires any amount of alterations before it is even pass- able. I. therefore marvel greatly at the fact that so many women content (themselves with the ready-made samples instead of paying a little more to have them made, or, better still, making their own blouses with the aid of a good pattern. In this way one can secure a better wearing article which is also characteristic looking, a qualification un- known to the ready-made blouses which arc turned out in quantities all alike. The pretty bodice depicted ' is suitable either for a dressy blpu.se or for the comple- tion of a dainty muslin or washing silk frock. It is made with a pointed lace collar which forms the semi-transparent yoke, some</p>
