      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-09-19_WidnesExaminer_art0069" n="art0069">
        <head>WEEKLY REPORT ON THE HEALTH OF WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>WEEKLY REPORT ON THE HEALTH OF WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>ENDING SEPTEMBER 12th, 1903. During I the week, the following Births and Deaths were registered :—Warrington Registration District births, 45 • deaths, 23. The excess of births overdeaths was 22. The birth-rate was equal to 34-8. The death-rate from all causes was equal to 17.7 per 1,000, against 18.8 the average of the previous 4 weeks and against 231 the corresponding period of last year' The death-rate from the seven chief zymotic diseases was equal to 6•1 per 1,000, against 4.9 the average rate of the previous 4 weeks and against 4•7 the corresponding period of 1902.</p>
        <p>The ages of mortality were:- 0-1 1-5 5-15 15-25 95-65 65-7-up. Total</p>
        <p>4 9 2 6 2 - 23 The deaths included 3 from measles, 51rom diarrhcen, 1 from tubercular diseases, 2from cancer, 2 from lung 7 diseases, 2 from heart diseases, 1 from accidents, from all other causes.</p>
        <p>The followings of infectious disease have been reported during t'i.e week :—Scarlet fever 6 cases' Total number of patients in hospital week ending 12th September. 40. METEOROLOGY.—The mean temperature was 52 and therefore seven degrees lower than the precedite? week. The maximum temperature 66 F., was record...4a, on the 6th lust, and the minimum temperature 38 r' on tie 6th inst</p>
        <p>_ The rainfall measured 2.81 inch. The general direc- tion was N.N.W.</p>
        <p>J. GUEST GORNALL. Medical Officer of Health.</p>
        <p>The Proposed New Church at Orford. The boxes in aid of the Church Building Fund have been opened and found to contain £8 13s. ld• addition promises to the amount of V-625 12s, WI; been already acknowledged. To this must be addea the promise of a site by Colonel Ireland-BlackbarFe,! which is at the present being carefully examined. w!tu,, a view to finding a good foundation for buildiv. purposes.</p>
      </div>
